{"name":"Balcony Rose","hex":"#e2bcb8","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"balcony","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An accessible structure extending from a building, especially outside a window.","An accessible structure overlooking a stage or the like."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/balcony"},{"term":"rose","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A shrub of the genus Rosa, with red, pink, white or yellow flowers.","A flower of the rose plant."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make rose-colored; to redden or flush.","To perfume, as with roses."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rose"}],"entries":[{"title":"Balcony","blocks":[{"text":"A balcony is a platform that typically projects from the wall of a building, supported by columns or console brackets, and enclosed with a balustrade, usually above the ground floor. They are commonly found on multi-level houses, apartments and buildings."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Overzicht_van_het_bovenste_deel_van_de_voorgevel_met_dakkapel_%28kajuit%29_en_balkon_-_Groningen_-_20387674_-_RCE.jpg/330px-Overzicht_van_het_bovenste_deel_van_de_voorgevel_met_dakkapel_%28kajuit%29_en_balkon_-_Groningen_-_20387674_-_RCE.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Balcony","wikidata":"Q170552"},{"title":"Rose","blocks":[{"text":"A rose is either a woody perennial flowering plant of the genus Rosa, in the family Rosaceae, or the flower it bears. There are over three hundred species and tens of thousands of cultivars. The plants range in size and form, from trailing and erect shrubs to climbers up to 7 metres (23 ft) in height. Sharp prickles appear on the stems of many species. Their flowers vary in size and shape and are usually large and showy, in colours ranging from white through pinks, reds, oranges and yellows."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/w